{%- set faqs = [
  ["What is a Security Architecture Review?", "A Security Architecture Review is an assessment of how an organization's IT systems are designed and how security controls protect applications and sensitive data. It helps identify design weaknesses and gaps that could expose business systems to cyber threats."],
  ["Why do businesses need Security Architecture Review Services?", "Businesses need security architecture reviews to identify risks in system design before they lead to security incidents. These assessments help organizations evaluate existing security controls and reduce the risk of unauthorized access or data exposure."],
  ["What does a Security Architecture Review include?", "A Security Architecture Review can include assessments of application architecture and network infrastructure along with cloud environments and identity management. The scope also covers security boundaries and data protection controls based on the organization's technology environment."],
  ["What is the difference between a Security Architecture Review and a Vulnerability Assessment?", "A Security Architecture Review evaluates the overall system design and how security controls work together. A vulnerability assessment focuses on identifying known security weaknesses in systems and applications. Both approaches offer different insights into an organization's security posture."],
  ["Which systems can be covered in a Security Architecture Review?", "The assessment can cover enterprise IT systems and cloud infrastructure along with web applications and APIs and hybrid environments. The exact scope depends on your architecture and business requirements."],
  ["How long does a Security Architecture Review take?", "The duration depends on the complexity of your IT environment and the number of systems included in the assessment. A focused review may take several days while a large enterprise environment may require several weeks."],
  ["What deliverables do you receive after a Security Architecture Review?", "Deliverables can include a security architecture review report and documented design weaknesses along with risk ratings and prioritized remediation recommendations. A security improvement roadmap may also be provided to guide future architectural changes."],
  ["Can a Security Architecture Review help with compliance requirements?", "Yes. A review can identify gaps between existing security controls and relevant framework requirements. Depending on the assessment scope, the review may support alignment with standards such as ISO 27001 and guidance such as the NIST Cybersecurity Framework, although the review itself does not establish compliance or certification."],
  ["When should an organization conduct a Security Architecture Review?", "A review is recommended when designing a new system or migrating to the cloud and when making major infrastructure changes. Periodic reviews also help identify architectural risks as applications and business requirements evolve."],
  ["How do Security Architecture Review Services improve long-term security?", "Security architecture reviews help businesses identify weaknesses in system design and address gaps in security controls. The resulting recommendations support better technology decisions and help organizations incorporate appropriate security measures into future system development and infrastructure changes."]
] %}

