<!-- PROCESS                                                              -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<section class="section section--ink" aria-labelledby="s5-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="process">
      <div class="process__aside">
        <h2 class="process__title" id="s5-title">How Our Security Architecture Review Works</h2>
        <p class="process__lede">CipherTrivia follows a structured Security Architecture Review process to identify design-level security gaps and assess how effectively your IT systems protect critical business assets. Our approach focuses on understanding your existing architecture and evaluating security controls before delivering practical recommendations to reduce risks.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="process__list" data-process>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Architecture Discovery and Scope Definition</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We begin by understanding your technology environment and business requirements to identify the systems and components included in the review. This helps define the assessment scope across applications and networks along with cloud infrastructure and access management.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Security Design and Control Assessment</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Our team reviews system architecture and security configurations to understand how applications communicate and how access to critical resources is managed. We examine security boundaries and data protection measures to identify weaknesses in the existing design.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Risk Identification and Impact Analysis</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Identified gaps are evaluated based on their severity and potential impact on business operations. We assess how architectural weaknesses could expose sensitive information or create opportunities for unauthorized access.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Findings Report and Remediation Roadmap</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We provide a structured report documenting security gaps and their potential consequences along with prioritized recommendations. The roadmap helps technical teams understand which improvements require immediate attention and how to address architectural risks.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Remediation Guidance and Review</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Following the assessment, we discuss key findings and recommended improvements with relevant stakeholders. Additional review activities can help validate proposed design changes and support the implementation of stronger security controls.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

